cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use BioSlice5X in research, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Also cite the underlying scientific work — the FRESH technique (Lee et al.
  2019 in Science) and the CHIPS construct (Shiwarski et al. 2025 in Science
  Advances) — when reporting work that depends on those methodologies.
title: "BioSlice5X: open-source 5-axis slicer for syringe bioprinting"
version: 0.1.1-dev
date-released: 2026-05-11
abstract: >-
  BioSlice5X is an open-source 5-axis slicer targeting syringe-based
  bioprinting in a yield-stress support bath (the FRESH/CHIPS workflow).
  It generates RepRapFirmware G-code for Open5X Prusa and Voron profiles
  with cell-viability-aware path validation, multi-syringe coordination,
  per-syringe spatial region selectors, and a 3D toolpath viewer with
  per-segment wall-shear-stress coloring and layer scrubbing.
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/alphadi10/bioslice5x"
keywords:
  - bioprinting
  - 5-axis
  - slicer
  - FRESH
  - CHIPS
  - bioink
  - cell viability
  - tissue engineering
  - open source
